/* book: lead: Active control technology (ACT) makes the flight control computers do more than follow the stick: they shape airframe loads and supply stability. Relaxing static stability lets the centre of gravity move aft, so the tail pushes down less and trim drag falls. Load alleviation cuts gust and manoeuvre peaks, so the wing can be lighter. Some syllabi call such an aircraft a control configured vehicle;  */
