/* book exam traps: FADEC does not move the thrust lever; the lever is the pilot's or auto-throttle's demand. | N1 is the fan or low-pressure spool and normally sets thrust; N2 is the high-pressure spool. | EGT is a limit, not the thrust-setting parameter: on a hot day the engine reaches its EGT or N1 limit at a lower thrust. | Using °C in θ = T1 ÷ 288.15. Use kelvin: 40 °C is 313.15 K, so θ = 1.0868. | A rating is a thrust schedule, not a fixed fuel flow. */
